```
- **Required interface:** `def redirect_request(self, req, fp, code, msg, headers, newurl)` — method of the retained class `YoutubeDLRedirectHandler(urllib.request.HTTPRedirectHandler)`. The retained class wires 301/303/307/308 to `HTTPRedirectHandler.http_error_302`; on a 301/302/303/307/308 response the standard-library redirect machinery calls this method and opens the returned request again through the same opener. No other name in the region is consumed outside it.
- **Observable behavior:** Determines the form of the follow-up request issued to the redirect target: its method, body, and header set.
- **Inputs:** `req` — the original request (its `headers` mapping, `get_method()`, `data`, `origin_req_host`, `full_url` are read); `fp` — response body; `code`/`msg` — status and reason phrase; `headers` — response headers; `newurl` — absolute URL.
- **Outputs and errors:** Returns a `urllib.request.Request` for `newurl` carrying the computed method; body `req.data` when the method is unchanged, `None` when it changed; headers derived from `req.headers`, without `Content-Length` or `Content-Type` when the method changed; `origin_req_host=req.origin_req_host`; `unverifiable=True`. Raises `urllib.error.HTTPError(req.full_url, code, msg, headers, fp)` for statuses outside 301/302/303/307/308.
- **Side effects and interactions:** The method performs no I/O; the redirect machinery opens the returned request through the same opener.
- **Required sequencing and state:** The method is decided first: 303 → `GET` unless the original method was `HEAD`; 301/302 with original `POST` → `GET`; otherwise the original method. Only when the follow-up method differs from the original is the body `None` and `Content-Length`/`Content-Type` dropped; otherwise the original body is carried.
- **Region boundary:** Self-contained — the range spans the entire method declaration. Mechanical consequences of the cut, not design: the retained text above supplies the class header and the `http_error_30x` aliases; the retained text below resumes at module level. The replacement must be exactly one method definition named `redirect_request` at class-body indentation, closing no other block and binding no name the retained text below references.
