It does not state expected outcomes or prescribe implementation structure.

## Reached at
  Two PHP classes of the Composer project tree at /app, resolved by the project'"'"'s
  own autoloader and driven in-process. Every calling program begins:
      require_once '"'"'/app/vendor/autoload.php'"'"';
      use Composer\Repository\Vcs\GitDriver;   // respectively Composer\Repository\Vcs\HgDriver
  The project'"'"'s composer.json maps the `Composer\` namespace PSR-4 to
  `src/Composer`, so the names resolve to
  `/app/src/Composer/Repository/Vcs/GitDriver.php` and
  `/app/src/Composer/Repository/Vcs/HgDriver.php`. Before any driver call, each
  program checks `(new ReflectionClass(GitDriver::class))->getFileName()`
  (realpath'"'"'d) lies under `/app/src/Composer`, so the classes must be defined in
  that tree — a copy of either class loaded from any other location is not
  reached. Callers run under the PHP 8.0 CLI at `/usr/local/bin/php`, invoked as
  `php -r '"'"'<inline PHP>'"'"'` with working directory `/app`.
  Both public methods reached on both classes route every VCS-tool invocation
  through the `Composer\Util\ProcessExecutor` instance handed to the constructor:
  the driver hands it a command string via `execute(...)` and splits listing
  output via `splitLines(...)`. That injected instance is the caller'"'"'s only
  observation point for the command strings the driver builds; the installed git
  and mercurial binaries are never executed on this path.

## Must provide
  Composer\Repository\Vcs\GitDriver   class, autoloadable under `Composer\`,
                                      extending the retained abstract base
                                      Composer\Repository\Vcs\VcsDriver
  Composer\Repository\Vcs\HgDriver    class, same arrangement
  __construct                         5 positional parameters (see Called as);
                                      currently the `final` constructor declared
                                      on the abstract base class
  getBranches()                       public method, no parameters, on both classes
  getFileContent($file, $identifier)  public method, two positional string
                                      parameters, on both classes
  repoDir                             declared instance property on both classes
                                      (currently `protected`), reachable via
                                      ReflectionClass::getProperty('"'"'repoDir'"'"')
  executor routing                    the VCS invocations inside getBranches()/
                                      getFileContent() must pass through the
                                      ProcessExecutor instance received at
                                      construction, not around it

