## Setup required
  - `/app/vendor/autoload.php` must exist with the project'"'"'s PSR-4 mapping
    (`Composer\` -> `src/Composer`); the project'"'"'s dependencies are already
    installed by the image build.
  - Runtime: PHP 8.0 CLI at `/usr/local/bin/php`; calling programs run with
    working directory `/app`.
  - The driver classes must load from the project tree under `/app/src/Composer`;
    a calling program aborts before any call if the reflection check resolves the
    class file anywhere else.

## Test harness boundary
  A pytest-driven runner executes each probe as a standalone PHP program through
  `subprocess`, running `/usr/local/bin/php -r '"'"'<inline script>'"'"'` with cwd
  `/app`. The inline script — the autoloader require, the reflection ownership
  check, driver construction, and every assertion — belongs to the calling side
  and is not part of the implementation; the engineer does not rebuild it.
  The caller injects a mock subclass of `Composer\Util\ProcessExecutor`. Its
  `execute()` records every command string the driver hands it in a public
  `$commands` array, then serves pre-registered output for any command containing
  one of the substrings '"'"'git branch'"'"', '"'"'git show'"'"' (git driver) or '"'"'hg branches'"'"',
  '"'"'hg bookmarks'"'"', '"'"'hg cat'"'"' (hg driver); any other command receives empty output.
  The mock never spawns a real git or hg process, so nothing a caller observes
  flows through anything other than the project-owned driver classes. The support
  classes the caller instantiates — Composer\Config, Composer\IO\NullIO,
  Composer\Util\HttpDownloader, and the Composer\Util\ProcessExecutor base class —
  are retained project code, not part of what is reconstructed.
